<%# Overall progress. Kept separate so a step landing does not re-render the whole page.

    `case` gets its own ERB tag and each `when` gets another. Squeezed into a single tag with inline
    `then` continuations it was unreadable, and Herb reports it as a parse error: a case with its
    conditions inside one tag cannot be reliably parsed, compiled or formatted.

    Careful in here: ERB comment delimiters do not nest, so writing a closing tag inside this text
    ends the comment early and the rest becomes markup. That is what broke this file once already. %>
<p class="status status--<%= analysis.status %>" id="analysis_status">
  <% case analysis.status %>
  <% when "pending" %>
    Queued…
  <% when "running" %>
    Running. Fast checks appear first; Common Crawl and the model probes take longer.
  <% when "done" %>
    Done<% if analysis.replayed? %>, replayed from cache<% end %>.
    <% if analysis.cost_millicents.positive? %>
      <small>Model spend: <%= (analysis.cost_millicents / 1000.0).round(3) %> dollars</small>
    <% end %>
  <% when "failed" %>
    Something failed. Partial results are shown below.
  <% end %>
</p>

<%# Measure it again from scratch.
    A cached result is the right default and the wrong answer whenever the cache is older than a fix
    to the probe: what you see then is a stale refusal wearing the clothes of a measurement, and no
    amount of reloading changes it, because the row stores what it stored.
    Offered only on a finished run, and only for a target we can rebuild. It spends real money every
    time, so it says so on the button rather than in a tooltip.

    A div, never a p. button_to renders a form, a form is not phrasing content, and the browser
    closes an open p when it meets one: the button and its explanation were hoisted out as siblings
    and the paragraph rendered empty. Same trap as the quota line above the examples. %>
<% if analysis.status.in?(%w[done failed]) %>
  <div class="status__again">
    <%= button_to "Re-run without cache", analyses_path, class: "analyzer__linkbtn",
          params: { docs_url: analysis.docs_url, repo: analysis.repo,
                    passage: analysis.passage, refresh: "1" } %>
    <small>Discards every cached check for this pair and measures it again. Costs
    <%= signed_in? ? "your budget" : "one of your free checks" %>, cached or not.</small>
  </div>
<% end %>
